\chapter{Independent type, memory, and advisory analysis}
\label{ch:89}
\index{Independent type, memory, and advisory analysis}
\index{LibStone!Chisel}
\index{LibStone!Nerotypical}

Nerotypical can independently validate a concrete structural HIR subset through its prepared solver SDK. Chisel checks lowered resource control flow for admitted ownership and loan profiles. Each requires a compatible optional build and can reject internal representations it cannot model. Wetstone's bounded advisory analysis and Syren reporting address a different job: informing the user and, in supported cases, proposing separately checked repairs.

\section{Interpret tool outcomes}
Use a valid scalar sample and a violation designed for each analysis. Include an unsupported feature so the test distinguishes failed validation, unavailable solver configuration, and a skipped advisory. A reported proof applies to the modeled obligations and input. A compiler-valid repair can still change user intent. Compare source differences and run a behavior oracle when adopting one. Keep the source checker, canonical verifier, optional analysis and native boundary in the report so readers know which component established each result.

